facts={1589:['PresentationPlugin owns one startup config; TacticalGraphicsSettings clone and DirectionalLightShadowMap derive same configured value during build. DefaultSettings obtains plugin default from same authored YAML, not second hardcoded configuration. Runtime configuration replacement is not promised by current setup-owned native resources. StartupTiming clock and reported flag are temporal diagnostic history, intentionally not derived current terrain readiness.','Actual schedule places celestial material updater after current celestial and pendingtrees, but does not bypass global unchanged gates; laternewtargets with unchanged inputs remain exactF042 conditional obligation. Grass interaction updater has independent schedule/stateF072. Full shader directive fixture walks two roots and is independent parser-order oracle, read only. Comments claiming shared capture/client setup do not constitute proof every binary adds identical externalplugins.'],1590:['Add obstacle observer derives native rock mesh/material from same immutable RockRecipe or queues tree presentation. Marker denotes lifecycle rather than duplicate current recipe. No normal in-place obstacle type mutation/rebuild route proved.','Review shoot selection uses source shoot_identity BEFORE local translation, then filters leaves by that source identity and applies same offset. Stable source biological identity is intentionally not recomputed from translated review coordinates; this avoids false stale-source-ID finding. Focus and preferred view derive current shifted branch/leaf geometry, distinct from original world root. Full source fixture analyzes canopy competition, no execution.'],1591:['RockField phase/sin/cos are private immutable per-operation coefficients computed together, so caching trig is explicit ownership, not separately mutable source. Conservative proxy sphere versus detailed surface are intentionally distinct collision/render approximations; field adds radial bound before extraction. Exact numeric operations and malformed recipe dimensions remain admission/operations obligations.','Rock flat lithology colour for other representation versus texture tint/roughness/macro response encode different material stages; no unjustified equality between them. Geometry and material currently use exact same named phase/seed formula but different numerical consumers; no source contract says every primitive optical coefficient must equal geometry amplitude. Current recipes immutable, no cache across editedrecipe inputs. Full319 source/fixture roles read.'],1592:['Independent gnarling controls intentionally separate causal growth dimensions, not cached gnarliness classification. Showcase entries are authored distinct policy, not duplicates of one current state. WoodyPlantForm plus generic parameters has MatureOak ignored-payload gapF075; other actual specialized branch geometry remains later unread.','TreeBranchSegment start/end/radii/depth/group/tip encode geometry/topology roles, not all derivable from one segment without whole graph. TreeCrownBounds recomputes branch endpoint reduction per requested predicate; empty filtered branch Inf/NaN remains existing admission/aggregate issue, not persistent duplicate bound cache. Transported frame retains previous axis as temporal continuity history rather than recomputing unstable reference eachring.'],1593:['Native leaf LODs derive from same TreeLeaf source but intentionally use different coverage expansion/card counts and torsion detail. Sparse1.9, card1.24 and cambered1.10 compensate distinct representation loss; not competing authored leaf dimensions. Both preserve biological petiole/root relation via offset adjustment; leaf shade/AO/shadowthreshold native lanes are distinct roles.','Source shootID and leafordinal retain source biological identity for deterministic LOD membership, not current mesh iteration. Bud filter identifies currentyear depth3 terminal branch purpose; group filtering uses same primarygroup. All505 source lines/fixture loops including exact50784/38088 topology/subset/shadow reference observations consumed, no run. Source arbitrary branch/leaf member correlations and native normalized basis issues remain independent lenses.'],1594:['Actual oak dispatch ignores generic supplied leaf parameters; fixed16/length/petiole equations provide parallel authorityF075. Beech/shrub consume supplied parameters and preserve deliberately different botanical morphology; no force allspecies share one sampling equation. Current canopy_competition ignored by oakleaf producer is explicit source behavior, not assumed alpha requirement.','Each leaf inherits groups and source shoot identity once from selected terminal source; petiole/center are different geometric features, length/width independently authored dimensions. right/up orientation vectors computed for valid producer, no arbitrary allfieldsorthonormal guarantee. Immutable seeds assigned by fixedpurpose per sourceleaf; source history ID preserved when native geometry later shifts.'],1595:['Source shoot identity is deterministic content-derived key from group and exact start/end bit coordinates, then retained to per-leaf entropy/selection. Identity scope is original source shoot, not globally unique durable tree/character identity, and64bit hash collisions not impossible. Absence of tree seed in local identity is deliberate shape-derived source key, no claim globalidentity uniqueness.'],1596:['Sparse and detailed selections are intentionally complementary different policies: retain one lane versus omit one lane. Both use canonical shootID+leafordinal and sort exact same source identity tuple, making reordering leaves irrelevant for unique normal identity set. Selection Vec is operation-local view of immutable source, not independently edited currentleaf roster. Duplicate forged identicalsortkeys could beorderunstable; no normal duplicate producer proved.'],1597:['Every literal names distinct leaf geometry/identity/shadow/retained/omitted random purpose. SHOOT_IDENTITY actual constant matches identity producer. No independently stored current decision or alias; exactpurpose strings part of deterministic source protocol.']}
